Apple TV appears to be unavailable for some users, following a recent outage of Apple Services that began on September 30.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/04/New-Apple-TV-Logo.jpeg" alt="" width="1600" height="901" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1043659" /><br/>
The original outage took down the App Store, Apple Fitness+, Apple Music, and several other services, but those are all now back online. Only Apple TV is still not working for an unknown number of users.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/support/systemstatus/">System Status page</a> indicates an ongoing issue with Apple TV that started on September 30 at 4:43 p.m. Eastern Time. "Some users are affected," the page says, adding "Apple TV may be unavailable due to scheduled maintenance."<br/>
